Source: qore-oracle-instantclient
Section: non-free/libs
Priority: optional
Maintainer: David Nichols <david@qore.org>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3, libaio-dev
Standards-Version: 4.7.4
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://www.oracle.com/database/technologies/instant-client.html
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-oracle.git
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/qoretechnologies/module-oracle/tree/develop/packaging/instantclient

Package: qore-oracle-instantclient23
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         qore-oracle-libaio-compat (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Oracle Instant Client 23 libraries for Qore integrations
 This package preserves Oracle's unmodified Basic distribution, including its
 OCI libraries, supporting data and license notices. It allows applications
 to connect to Oracle Database without a full database installation.
 The vendor libraries are proprietary and cannot be rebuilt from source.

Package: qore-oracle-instantclient23-dev
Section: non-free/libdevel
Architecture: amd64
Depends: qore-oracle-instantclient23 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Oracle Instant Client 23 development kit for Qore integrations
 This package preserves Oracle's unmodified SDK headers, tools and examples.
 The SDK is needed to compile applications and Qore's Oracle database driver.
 It is installed beside the corresponding Basic distribution.

Package: qore-oracle-libaio-compat
Section: non-free/libs
Architecture: amd64
Depends: libaio1t64 (>= 0.3.113-8), ${misc:Depends}
Conflicts: libaio1
Description: amd64 libaio SONAME compatibility link for Oracle Instant Client
 Oracle Instant Client requires libaio.so.1. Debian and Ubuntu provide the
 compatible ABI under libaio.so.1t64. This package owns the compatibility
 symlink and depends on the system library; it contains no library copy.
